# ── Database (Postgres) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Production (Vercel): a hosted Postgres connection string. The app creates
# and seeds the tables automatically on first run. Recommended providers:
#   • Neon — https://neon.tech (free tier, serverless)
#   • Vercel Postgres — https://vercel.com/marketplace/neon (same thing, managed)
# Example: postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=

# Without DATABASE_URL the app falls back to a local SQLite file (fine for
# dev) — on Vercel that means an ephemeral demo database in /tmp.

# ── Paystack ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get your keys at https://dashboard.paystack.com → Settings → API Keys & Webhooks
# Test mode keys start with sk_test_ / pk_test_ (use Paystack test cards for free testing)
# Live mode keys start with sk_live_ / pk_live_ (switch on in Paystack dashboard)
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Without Paystack keys the app runs in PAYSTACK DEMO MODE:
# the card checkout simulates a successful payment and is clearly labelled as a demo.
